-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b265dacaa48431c73458345f7b891a62b3d1b4b2a6c11e"} {"question" "q-79285" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3"] ["math" "x=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=6\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2"] ["math" "x=25\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2,\\,y=9\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3"] ["math" "x=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -2"] ["math" "x=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b265dacaa48431c73458345f7b891a62b3d1b4b2a6c11e"} {"question" "q-79285" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b265dacaa48431c73458345f7b891a62b3d1b4b2a6c11e"} {"question" "q-79292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/assets/7d45616d089e8f5d078ff48c949b26d0920074ab4b611ec71b491a0e18fd293c.png)\n\nConsider the ellipse centered at $(3,1)$ with horizontal radius $1$ and vertical radius $2,$ as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the ellipse once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(4,1)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b265dacaa48431c73458345f7b891a62b3d1b4b2a6c11e"} {"question" "q-79292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the point $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +h,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +k,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the ellipse is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(h+a,k).$\n\nIn our case, the ellipse is centered at the point $(3,1),$ $a=1$ and $b=2.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b265dacaa48431c73458345f7b891a62b3d1b4b2a6c11e"} {"question" "q-79292" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4be40ac811c9a7849b7e9caf70e564b541ed013e8fe8332c47f598abf0a761c5"} {"question" "q-79292" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b265dacaa48431c73458345f7b891a62b3d1b4b2a6c11e"} {"question" "q-79292" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1"] ["math" "x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1,\\,y=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3"] ["math" "x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +1,\