operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +k,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the ellipse is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(h+a,k).$\n\nIn our case, the ellipse is centered at the point $(-2,1),$ $a=4$ and $b=5.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b265dacaa48431c73458345f7b891a62b3d1b4b2a6c11e"} {"question" "q-327172" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4be40ac811c9a7849b7e9caf70e564b541ed013e8fe8332c47f598abf0a761c5"} {"question" "q-327172" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b265dacaa48431c73458345f7b891a62b3d1b4b2a6c11e"} {"question" "q-327172" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\cos(\\theta)-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b265dacaa48431c73458345f7b891a62b3d1b4b2a6c11e"} {"question" "q-327172" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b2