emy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b265dacaa48431c73458345f7b891a62b3d1b4b2a6c11e"} {"question" "q-106399" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4be40ac811c9a7849b7e9caf70e564b541ed013e8fe8332c47f598abf0a761c5"} {"question" "q-106399" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b265dacaa48431c73458345f7b891a62b3d1b4b2a6c11e"} {"question" "q-106399" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=14\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2"] ["math" "x=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2"] ["math" "x=7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -3"] ["math" "x=7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2"] ["math" "x=7\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -2"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b265dacaa48431c73458345f7b891a62b3d1b4b2a6c11e"} {"question" "q-106399" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=7\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -3,\\,y=4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b265dacaa48431c73458345f7b891a62b3d1b4b2a6c11e"} {"question" "q-106403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/assets/5b344621d5500d3253295c970b0a7557b80f4d2cbfa66c17ba6f8868c1424c08.png)\n\nThe quarter-ellipse above is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nWhat is the domain of the parameter $\\theta ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b265dacaa48431c73458345f7b891a62b3d1b4b2a6c11e"} {"question" "q-106403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The parametric equations of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ are\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=b\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $a=2$ and $b=3.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the *full* ellipse are\n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nTo restrict the parameterization to a quarter-ellipse, we associate the parameter $\\theta $ with the central angle formed by a point $(x,y)$ on the elipse and the $x$-axis. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/assets/9e236591e21403bb739dafa68a665c8a10eed0e9e8ac104e7b39431f02329c17.png)\n\nWe can see that if we restrict $\\theta $ to $[\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]$, we get the quarter-ellipse.\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the quarter-ellipse are \n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b265dacaa48431c73458345f7b891a62b3d1b4b2a6c11e"} {"question" "q-106403" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4be40ac811c9a7849b7e9caf70e564b541ed013e8fe8332c47f598abf0a761c5"} {"question" "q-106403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b265dacaa48431c73458345f7b891a62b3d1b4b2a6c11e"} {"question" "q-106403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]"] ["math" "\\theta \\in [0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}]"] ["math" "\\theta \\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},2\\pi ]"] ["math" "\\theta \\in [\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\pi ]"] ["math" "\\theta \\in [\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b265dacaa48431c73458345f7b891a62b3d1b4b2a6c11e"} {"question" "q-106403" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\theta \\in [\\pi ,\\frac{3\\pi }{2}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/state.json" "file_sha256" "e20cb2359147782169b265dacaa48431c73458345f7b891a62b3d1b4b2a6c11e"} {"question" "q-79275" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040724/assets/cbe1a9cf99e5a3b2cae80a4bfd01cdcabdc77560ccbb17ff9c7